 "text": "9/29/26, 9:42 AM\n\n2                                                10\nREQ. Fact |mnnnnnnnnanannnnnnnnnnnnnenn amen nncnnne | ane nnnnennnennn cnnnnene nr\n\n|_|\nZ                   C          Y                                   P\n08                   02                    10           09                                    01\n\n4,000 5,000                                                           kWh/Year\nPerCons.... |\u2014\u20144\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014_----\n\nMR Result 0          900        720 800                    ? kWh\n\u2014\u2014\n|\n\nMR Reas.\n\nWght. Unit                           200        100              600\n\nWght. Por.                            20%      10%             60%\n\nOn installation of the device, a period consumption value of 4000 kWh/year is entered for the register. This value is changed to\n5,000 kWh / year for the period 08 to 02.\n\nThe minimum portion of weighting in percent is 30%.\nThe sum of the weighting units for one year is 1,000.\n\nWith a weighting portion of 10%, period O09 to 10 is not representative. The system goes back to the next meter reading result\n02. With 30%, the period 09 to O02 is representative, however, the period consumption was not changed within this period.\n\nTherefore, extrapolation is based on the on the meter reading results rather then the period consumption:\n\n1. Determination of meter reading difference 09 to 02: (800 kWh 720 kWh) + (720 kWh 500 kWh) = 300 kWh\n\n2. Determination of consumption for 09 by multiplying the meter reading difference with the register factor: 300 kWh2 =\n600 kWh\n\n3. Determination of consumption per weighting unit: 600 kWh : 300 = 2 kWh\n\n4. Extrapolation of consumption for period 09 to O01: 2 kWh600 = 1,200 kWh\n\n5. Determination of the meter reading difference for period O09 to O1 by dividing the consumption value by the register\nfactor: 1,200 kWh: 10 = 120 kWh\n\n6. Determination of the expected meter reading for O01 by adding the meter reading difference for meter reading 09: 800\nkWh + 120 kWh = 920 kWh\n\nThe expected meter reading at time P is 920 kWh.\n\nSe Example\n\nExample 5: Forecasts from previous periods and changes to period consumption values in the forecast period\n",
